name c01m10-wolfpack
timeout 600
time 1992-10-29T19:48:00Z

# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992), CAMPAIGN ONE "OPERATION MAXIMUM OVERKILL",
# MISSION 10 OF 10 -- {Wolfpack}*1 [MIS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/comanche/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [MIS]: 12 ground goals -- 4 T-80s and 8 Geckos -- while 8 Werewolves that are NOT goals
# hunt the player, who carries exactly 8 Stingers. "You have one Stinger for each Werewolf, so Don't
# Miss!"
#
# THE FIELD [MIS]: map 4 (Khash Rud, Afghanistan, terrain.md 6), night -- sun -71.56 deg at the
# lead's spawn, computed by the runner. 12 starred objects, unlock marker *1.
# THE CAST: 8 Werewolf -> `ah64` - 12 T-80 -> `target_hard` - 8 Gecko -> `sa8` - wingman -> `f16`.
# THE LOADOUT [MIS]: cannon 500, rockets 62, Hellfire 8, Stinger 8, artillery 0, wingman 12, fuel
# 12000. Declared here: 4 x `mk82`, 4 x `aim9`, gun 500, `set fuel_int_pct 60` = 12000 against the
# campaign's own maximum of 20 000. The rockets and the artillery have no row and no mechanism;
# the truncation of the other two is the F-16's nine pylons.

# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES ARE STATED IN FULL IN c01m01-werewolves-on-patrol.fbm AND APPLY HERE
# ---- UNCHANGED: D1 no rotorcraft (the RAH-66 flies as `module f16`, 300 kt because 180-275 kt crash
# ---- the egress) - D2 the Werewolf is an `ah64` mover and fires nothing, ever - D3 flat 0 m ground,
# ---- because one mod carries one DEM and this campaign needs four theatres - D4 the clock is checked
# ---- against the logged sun elevation - D5 the anchoring is terrain.md's reconstruction and the
# ---- campaign names no place - D6 the striker spawns on the bearing to its aim point, because the
# ---- attack phase cannot fly itself onto its own run-in - D7 one striker is one aim point.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `lead`'s.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires the 12 ground goals. The 8 Werewolves are not goals, but the loadout
#   carries exactly 8 Stingers, so a run that spends Stingers on anything else and still wins would
#   have found a hole in the Stinger model. MEASURED: no Stinger is ever spent. The Werewolves cannot
#   be engaged (D2) and nothing else in the mission is an air target, so the `aim9` rack is carried and
#   never used -- the mission's title claim is untestable in this tree.
#   exit 3 = the expected reading; report the met count against 12.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`): TWO OF TWELVE, and the closest the SA-8 comes all campaign.
#   t = 21.3 / 24.5 s   two Mk-82 away, aimErrM 4.89 and 17.96; g01 and g02 destroyed
#   t = 32 launches     closest approach 6.84 m and 8.53 m against a 6 m fuze. The campaign's threat is
#                       one metre of geometry away from being real, at 150 m, at night
#   verdict             `lead` TIMEOUT, 2 of 12 met, `survive` met; `two` SUCCESS.
#   8 Stingers declared, 4 `aim9` carried, 0 fired: no Werewolf can be engaged (D2).

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight m10 1
  spawn 31.79188 63.00548 150 274.3 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 60
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 4 mk82
  set store 6 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 8 aim9
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 500
  set cmds_mode auto
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 31.79440 62.96617 150 300
  wp 31.79670 62.93025 1000 300
  objective kill unit t01
  objective kill unit t02
  objective kill unit t03
  objective kill unit t04
  objective kill unit g01
  objective kill unit g02
  objective kill unit g03
  objective kill unit g04
  objective kill unit g05
  objective kill unit g06
  objective kill unit g07
  objective kill unit g08
  objective survive

